secret.description:
GitLab (`X-Gitlab-Token`) and Buildkite (`X-Buildkite-Token`) send this value as is;
Jenkins and `CodePipeline` send it as `X-Watchtower-Token` (or `Authorization: Bearer`),
Azure Pipelines as the basic-auth password of the service hook.

kind.description:
`browser_extension`, `legacy_browser`, `localhost`, `web_crawler`, `handled_4xx` (the
"ignore handled 4xx" template: handled exceptions of 4xx responses) are switches, no value;
or `error_message`, `release` (glob) and `ip_range` (CIDR), which take a value.

app_ids.description:
Up to 50 mobile app ids (`com.example.app`): the iOS bundle id or Android package name the
mobile SDKs send in `X-Watchtower-App-Id`. Checked only on requests without an `Origin`;
empty (the default) refuses them.
